{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Symmetric","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.vacuumRow_conj_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.vacuumRow_conj_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L173-L182","doc":"**The vacuum row is charge-conjugation invariant.**  Because the quantum dimensions are self-dual\n(`d_q(λ′) = d_q(λ)`, corpus `qDim_conj`), the vacuum S-matrix row `S_{0λ} = d_q(λ)/D` is fixed by the\ntranspose involution `λ ↦ λ′`.  So the value-map target lives in the `C = +1` (self-dual) sector,\nwhere `S² = +1` and the real symmetric `S` has eigenvalues `±1` — the sector in which the PF-positive\n`+1` ground state is `d_q`.  (Restates, at the vacuum row, the sector the narrowing selects.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.eigenvalue_selfdual_sector_pm_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.eigenvalue_selfdual_sector_pm_one","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L151-L169","doc":"**Self-dual sector: eigenvalues are `±1`.**  Over a field, a nonzero eigenvector `w` that also\nlies in the `C = +1` (self-dual) sector — `C w = w` — has `ζ² = 1`, i.e. `ζ = ±1`.  This is the\ntightening of the global `ζ⁴ = 1` on the sector where the vacuum row lives\n(`vacuumRow_conj_invariant`): the real symmetric `S²` acts as `+1` there, so the PF-positive ground\neigenvalue is `+1` and its eigenvector is `d_q` (input (A)+(B), Ocneanu/Wenzl — cited, not proved). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.eigenvalue_pow_four_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.eigenvalue_pow_four_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L133-L149","doc":"**Eigenvalue narrowing: `ζ⁴ = 1`.**  Over a **field**, any eigenvalue `ζ` of `S` on a **nonzero**\nvector `v` is a 4th root of unity.  So the eigenfunctions the framework needs are not an arbitrary\northogonal family: their eigenvalues are the four charge-conjugation phases (as ordinary self-dual\nFourier forces `iⁿ` on Hermite functions).  On the self-dual (`C`-fixed) sector this tightens to\n`ζ = ±1`, and the PF-positive `+1` ground state is `d_q` (input (A)+(B), Ocneanu/Wenzl). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.eigenvector_pow_four_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.eigenvector_pow_four_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L114-L129","doc":"**Eigenvector action of `S⁴`: `ζ⁴ • v = v`.**  From `S⁴ = 1`, an eigenvector `v` with\n`S v = ζ v` satisfies `ζ⁴ • v = v` (over any `CommRing`, no nonzero hypothesis).  The scalar\nconsequence `ζ⁴ = 1` needs a nonzero `v` over a field — see `eigenvalue_pow_four_eq_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.conjFixed_sSq_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.conjFixed_sSq_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L106-L112","doc":"**On the self-dual sector `S² = +1`.**  A charge-conjugation-fixed vector `w` (`C w = w`,\nthe `C = +1` sector where the vacuum row lives) satisfies `S² w = w`: `S` restricted to the\nself-dual sector is an involution.  This is the sector statement behind the `±1` eigenvalue\ntightening (`eigenvalue_selfdual_sector_pm_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.sSq_mul_sSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.sSq_mul_sSq","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L102-L104","doc":"`S² * S² = 1` (the two-step form of self-reciprocality, `C² = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.sTransform_pow_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.sTransform_pow_four","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L93-L100","doc":"**Spectral self-reciprocality: `S⁴ = 1`.**  From `S² = C` and `C² = 1` the transform has order\ndividing 4 — the categorical avatar of a self-reciprocal (q-Hankel–type) transform `𝓗⁴ = id`.  This\nis the *structural* fact the value-map program should have been matching against, in place of screening\nnode values of an imported q-Bessel family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.C_invol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.C_invol","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L87-L87","doc":"Charge conjugation is an involution `C² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.S_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.S_sq","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L85-L85","doc":"**Self-duality** `S² = C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.S_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.S_symm","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L83-L83","doc":"`S` is symmetric (Frobenius self-duality of the pairing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.C","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The charge-conjugation matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.S","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The modular S-matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.SelfDualSTransform","kind":"structure","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing.lean#L73-L87","doc":"**A self-dual S-transform** on a finite fusion-label type.  Bundles the modular data used by the\nnarrowing: a symmetric matrix `S`, a charge-conjugation matrix `C` that is an involution, and the\nself-duality relation `S² = C`.  (In a modular tensor category `S` is symmetric and `S² = C` is the\nstandard modular relation; `C` is the charge-conjugation permutation, `C² = 1`.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}